Accounts Payable Clerk (20 to 32 hours) 20262853 
 - SALARY INDICATION In consultation - JOB GROUP Finance - JOB POSTING NUMBER 720262853 - LOCATION Eindhoven ABOUT THIS JOB OPENING 
Job Description 
You're good at distinguishing between main and secondary financial issues and can handle stress well. You're results-oriented, productive, and excel in a high-pressure environment. You enjoy working both independently and as part of a team. Your colleagues describe you as a hard worker who sets priorities well, is helpful, communicates clearly, and adapts quickly. You take the initiative and are passionate about your work. 
Job Requirements: 
· Process purchase invoices and post expenses based on invoices; 
· Process incoming and outgoing payments; 
· Manage suspense accounts and flag any discrepancies; 
· Serve as the point of contact for financial issues raised by various internal 
stakeholders; 
· You ensure the accurate and timely processing and verification of daily 
bank transactions and payment flows. 
· You provide support to the finance department with various tasks; 
· You assist with financial reviews and the collection of necessary documentation 
for reports and audits. 
· Other related tasks. 
Required skills: 
· MBO+ level (accounting) 
· Accurate, analytical, and meticulous in handling processes 
· You have a good command of Dutch and English (both spoken and 
written); 
· You can work both independently and as part of a team; 
· You are honest and reliable; 
· You are available for 20 to 32 hours per week; 
· Strong communication skills and a sense of responsibility; 
· Strong numerical skills and a solution-oriented mindset; 
· You are a team player and take a problem-solving approach; 
· You are comfortable working with ERP systems (preferably Afas);

(Administrative) logistics employee (2-shifts) 
 Logistiek en Supply chain Administratief en Secretarieel 36 - 40 uur 2500 - 3000 EUR 3000 - 3500 EUR 
 Introduction You do not let a single pallet go through without having seen it. It does not go into the warehouse until you have put the sticker on it. 
 What are you going to do? 
You are the one where the inbound process starts. Once the container is at the dock, you will check if it is the right one. Furthermore, you will 
Check the weight, length and width of the article; 
Check that all items are present in the container; 
Communicate deviations when they occur to your coordinator; 
You adjust deviations, with permission from your supervisor; 
Helps stack pallets; 
Check full pallets, drive them away with an EPT and make sure they are sealed. 
You also ensure that your team is and remains motivated; together we are strong! 
 This is what you get in return! 
We offer a competitive salary of 15,47€ per hour excluding 12,5% shift allowance. 
You can start right away and if everything goes well, more options could be available. 
 This is you! 
Do you have a positive attitude; 
Your communication skills are on point; 
Do you know how to carry out proper checks; 
Do you have experience as a logistics employee; 
Are you fluent in English; 
Do you get excited about working two shifts; 
Do you have an EPT certificate or are willing to get one; 
In addition to English and Dutch, do you also speak Polish? Then do not hold back and respond! 
 Here's where you'll get to work: Our client is one of the biggest retail suppliers in Europe. They are a regional giant with countless opportunities. 
